## AF action tools
- Some AF tools run in the background; their result says they started. End your turn then; the outcome arrives later as a host notice.
- An AF tool result may end with an `<af_state_update>` block: that is the new SOP state; follow it. It repeats the whole active-SOP block when another SOP became active (or what surrounds it changed), else it gives only the status and next step of the SOP you already know.

## Reading SOP guidance
SOP guidance uses an older tool notation. Translate it: `proposal-selection --experiment-hub` means `mcp__af__proposal_selection` with `experiment_hub: true`; a "conversation tool" it names is the AF question tool of that name; hyphens become underscores; `--flag value` becomes the argument `flag`; "set `output` to X" means `output: ["X"]`; an SOP command such as `/sop <name>` or `/resume_sop` means the matching tool under "SOP control" (or, where there is none, a command for the user to send). The af_context lists the active SOP's required tools by their names here.
